{"id":"H2124","lemma":"זִיזָא","transliteration":"ziza","sayIt":"zi-ZA","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Ziza","meaning":"A man of the tribe of Simeon(?) living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.37;\nson of: Shiphi (H8230)\n§ Ziza = \"shining\"\n1) son of Shiphi, a chief of the Simeonites in the reign of Hezekiah\n2) son of Rehoboam by Maachah the granddaughter of Absalom","glosses":["ziza"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"1ch-4","v":37,"renderings":{"bsb":"and Ziza","kjv":"And Ziza"}},{"chapterId":"2ch-11","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"Ziza","kjv":"and Ziza"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"1 Chronicles 4:37","note":"and Ziza the son of Shiphi, the son of Allon, the son of Jedaiah, the son of Shimri, the son of Shemaiah—","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Chronicles 11:20","note":"After her, he took Maacah the daughter of Absalom; and she bore him Abijah, Attai, Ziza, and Shelomith.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H0029","lemma":"אֲבִיָּה","transliteration":"aviyyah","gloss":"Abijah"},{"id":"H2093","lemma":"זָ֑הַם","transliteration":"zaham","gloss":"Zaham"},{"id":"H8230","lemma":"שִׁפְעִי","transliteration":"shiphi","gloss":"Shiphi"},{"id":"H7346","lemma":"רְחַבְעָם","transliteration":"rechavam","gloss":"Rehoboam"},{"id":"H4601","lemma":"מַעֲכָה","transliteration":"maakhah","gloss":"Maacah"},{"id":"H6262","lemma":"עַתַּי","transliteration":"attay","gloss":"Attai"},{"id":"H8019","lemma":"שְׁלֹמִית","transliteration":"shelomit","gloss":"Shelomith"},{"id":"H3266","lemma":"יְעוּשׁ","transliteration":"yeush","gloss":"Jeush"}],"senses":[{"id":"H2124H","gloss":"Ziza","relation":"H2124H ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}